  "title": "Aleijadinho (Antônio Francisco Lisboa)",
  "summary": "Aleijadinho, born Antônio Francisco Lisboa, was a colonial Brazilian sculptor and architect of Minas Gerais. A disabling illness appeared in 1777. His works include São Francisco de Assis church in Ouro Preto and, at Congonhas, statues of twelve prophets in soapstone carved from 1800 to 1805.",
